WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.484
I'm Yu Yao-Hsing.

00:00:01.484 --> 00:00:05.887
I study random matrix theory, and with AI writing the code, I ship real apps.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.992
I'm a high-school student in Taipei,

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:11.260
and I want to make everything pocket-sized, through the iPad.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.099
Seven years, from self-study to research:

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.014
studying high-dimensional noise through eigenvalues,

00:00:17.014 --> 00:00:19.544
to read noisy medical images reliably.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.554
My paper, on the limiting spectral distributions of random matrices,

00:00:23.554 --> 00:00:27.267
is published in the Cambridge Journal for Junior Scientists.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.805
The work behind it took bronze at the S.-T. Yau Science Award, in Beijing.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.658
That result became EigenDenoise:

00:00:35.658 --> 00:00:40.645
on-device image denoising and spectral analysis, based on random matrix theory.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.449
ManimStudio is a complete, offline Python animation studio for the iPad and iPhone.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.778
Whisper turns speech into accurate text, entirely on your device,

00:00:51.778 --> 00:00:54.426
and now composes music from a description.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.560
SidecarBridge turns an iPad into a private viewer and remote for your Mac.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.673
When GPS is lost, Force Velocity still draws the route: in a car from how it shakes,

00:01:06.673 --> 00:01:10.300
and in the air from the typical speed of real airline flights.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.007
Real downloads, counted by each store: over four thousand for the apps,

00:01:17.007 --> 00:01:19.861
and over seven thousand for my Python packages.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.187
A full Python runtime for iOS with real PyTorch, App Store safe;

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:29.445
Metal GPU acceleration for it; and whole operating systems booting in a browser.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.596
py2bin turns Python into machine code using nothing but the Python standard library,

00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:36.538
so it even runs on an iPad.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.620
Last, typhoons.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.608
Trackformer 1.2 forecasts the surrounding sea-level pressure and a moving

00:01:42.608 --> 00:01:47.160
storm core together, five days ahead, from data that ends at the issue time.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.588
I believe impossible is often just an assumption waiting to be challenged,

00:01:51.588 --> 00:01:54.557
and I want to bring new possibilities into people's hands.

00:01:54.557 --> 00:01:57.578
I'll keep challenging it, one iPad at a time, for everyone.

00:01:57.578 --> 00:01:58.848
I'm Yu Yao-Hsing.
